<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section__header">
      <span class="section__label">Sustainability</span>
      <div class="accent-line"></div>
      <h2 class="section__title">Eco-Friendly Fabric Options for Dog Coats</h2>
    </div>
    
    <div class="text-content">
      <p>Sustainable dog coats usually mean one of two changes: recycled fill material or organic cotton lining. Both are available without changing the core construction or the fit of the coat.</p>
      
      <p><strong>Recycled polyester fill and shell fabric</strong> (GRS certified) performs identically to virgin polyester in terms of warmth and water resistance | the recycling happens at the fibre stage, so there's no trade-off in coat performance. This is the easiest sustainability upgrade for insulated and puffer-style coats.</p>
      
      <p><strong>Organic cotton lining</strong> (GOTS certified) works well for fleece-alternative linings in mild-climate coats, though it doesn't perform the same insulating role as polyester fleece in cold-weather designs. We'll tell you directly if an organic cotton request doesn't suit your target climate rather than selling you a fabric that won't perform.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section__header">
      <span class="section__label">Before You Brief Us</span>
      <div class="accent-line"></div>
      <h2 class="section__title">What to Include in Your Dog Coat Design Brief</h2>
    </div>
    
    <div class="text-content">
      <p>A complete brief on the first email cuts a full round off the sampling timeline. Here's what we need to give you an accurate quote on the first response:</p>
      
      <ul class="product-list">
        <li class="product-list__item">Target breed(s) or general size range (toy, small, medium, large, giant)</li>
        <li class="product-list__item">Coat type | rain shell, fleece, insulated puffer, or harness vest</li>
        <li class="product-list__item">Belly coverage | back-only or full wrap-around</li>
        <li class="product-list__item">Closure preference | velcro, buckle, or snap (or "you decide")</li>
        <li class="product-list__item">Waterproofing requirement, if any, and target water column rating</li>
        <li class="product-list__item">Target retail price point, so we can recommend fabric within your margin</li>
        <li class="product-list__item">Branding needs | label type, logo application, packaging</li>
        <li class="product-list__item">Estimated quantity per size for your first order</li>
      </ul>
      
      <p>Don't have answers to all of these yet? Send what you have. We'll ask the rest and walk you through anything you're unsure about | this list is meant to speed things up, not gate the conversation.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="section" id="section-faq">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section__header">
      <span class="section__label">FAQ</span>
      <div class="accent-line"></div>
      <h2 class="section__title">Dog Coat Manufacturer | Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    </div>
    
    <div style="max-width: 800px;">
      
      <div class="faq-item" role="region">
        <button class="faq-item__question" aria-expanded="false">
          What is the minimum order quantity for custom dog coats?
          <span class="faq-item__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-item__answer" hidden>
          <p>300 pieces per style. That number can be split across sizes within one design | for example 60 extra small, 100 small, 100 medium, 40 large still counts as one style at 300 units. A separate colourway of the same pattern is usually treated as the same style, but a different fabric or a different cut counts as a new style.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      
      <div class="faq-item" role="region">
        <button class="faq-item__question" aria-expanded="false">
          What waterproof rating should a dog rain coat have?
          <span class="faq-item__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-item__answer" hidden>
          <p>3,000mm water column rating handles light to moderate rain and is the minimum we recommend for any coat marketed as waterproof. 5,000mm or higher holds up in sustained heavy rain and is what we use for premium outdoor lines. Anything under 1,500mm is closer to water-resistant than waterproof and should not be marketed as a rain coat.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      
      <div class="faq-item" role="region">
        <button class="faq-item__question" aria-expanded="false">
          How do you size dog coats for different breeds?
          <span class="faq-item__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-item__answer" hidden>
          <p>We grade by chest girth and back length together, not by weight alone. A Dachshund and a French Bulldog can weigh the same but need completely different proportions | long, narrow body versus short, broad chest. Breed-specific blocks for short-back, deep-chest, and standard proportions are available on request at no extra pattern cost.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      
      <div class="faq-item" role="region">
        <button class="faq-item__question" aria-expanded="false">
          Velcro, buckle, or snap closure | which is best for dog coats?
          <span class="faq-item__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-item__answer" hidden>
          <p>Velcro is fastest to put on but wears out after roughly 300 to 500 open-close cycles and snags on long-haired breeds. Side-release buckles last longer and adjust precisely but take a few seconds more to fasten. Snap closures sit in between on speed and durability. We recommend buckles for daily-wear coats and velcro only for occasional-use or costume pieces.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      
      <div class="faq-item" role="region">
        <button class="faq-item__question" aria-expanded="false">
          How long does dog coat sampling take?
          <span class="faq-item__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-item__answer" hidden>
          <p>7 to 14 calendar days from a confirmed design brief, depending on whether the fabric is in stock or needs sourcing. Sampling is free and we revise up to 10 times at no extra charge. Bulk cutting does not start until you approve the final sample in writing.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

